Go get what you really want.
I want more. Anyone more.

5
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,837
Come on, open up the door.

6
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:16,060
It's my life. It's your life.

7
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:17,748
Run like a wind, jump high.

8
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:18,710
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

9
00:00:18,793 --> 00:00:19,700
I know you're strong.

10
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:22,137
Believe you can achieve your goal.

11
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:24,600
Let's keep on going on the stage.

12
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:47,457
Let's do it again, you
know what I mean, baby.

13
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:50,037
No one can make my dream come true!

14
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:51,240
Don't you feel it?

15
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:55,197
I really don't know what is
Something is testing me every day.

16
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:56,557
Hey, let's go.

17
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:57,477
Let's fly away.

18
00:00:57,560 --> 00:01:00,577
I know I never wanna come back here.

19
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:01,797
Hey, let's go.

20
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:05,597
Let's fly away the great
end of the unknown rules.

21
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:07,437
Standing up, blowing up.

22
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:09,617
My dream is getting wilder.

23
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:12,617
I'm not afraid, beat me, hit me.

24
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:15,117
I will never turn around.

25
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:17,917
Another day, another chance.

26
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,097
You know it's never too late.

27
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:23,580
If I can't do it, so can you only without.

28
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:28,477
It's my life, it's your life.

29
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:31,557
Party for tomorrow, go
get what you really want.

30
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:35,580
I want more, anyone more,
come on, open up the door.

31
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:38,917
It's my life, it's your life.

32
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,957
Run like a wind, jump high, yeah, yeah.

33
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,597
I know you're strong.

34
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:45,137
Believe you cannot achieve your goal.

35
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:47,077
Let's keep on going, roaring.

36
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:49,337
It's my life, it's your life.

37
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:52,477
Fighting for your eyes that
I want, but your weary ones.

38
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:57,337
I want more, anyone more,
come on, open up the gate.

39
00:01:57,420 --> 00:02:01,537
It's my life, it's your light,
shine like a star to be good.

40
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:06,257
I know you're strong, just that
you can't achieve your best.

41
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:08,600
Let's keep on going out of day.

42
00:02:15,620 --> 00:02:19,020
You make my day every day.

43
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:56,460
No! This way!

44
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:04,780
We've got to get to the
center of town! Keep going!

45
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:29,116
Those buildings are getting
dragged across the ground!

46
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:32,900
And they're coming straight for us! Run!

47
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:37,597
The kingdom's getting crushed into a ball!

48
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,915
And us along with it!

49
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:53,197
The birdcage is shrinking.

50
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:55,577
That would explain the mass panic.

51
00:03:55,660 --> 00:03:59,537
The birdcage buries everything.

52
00:03:59,620 --> 00:04:03,577
Honey, this is a nightmare!

53
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:06,040
I see the battle isn't over yet.

54
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:09,697
I found honey again.

55
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:10,937
This is really happening.

56
00:04:11,020 --> 00:04:14,857
I'm not gonna sit here picking my
nose waiting for death to come.

57
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:18,157
Go find our fallen
allies—get them back up.

58
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:19,197
All right.

59
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:20,110
If

60
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:24,937
the battle goes on for too long, even
this plateau will be cut to pieces.

61
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:25,850
What

62
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:29,357
I thought this was the middle
of the kingdom isn't it?

63
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:30,270
The safest place?

64
00:04:30,353 --> 00:04:31,183
Look above.

65
00:04:31,266 --> 00:04:32,096
The

66
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:35,277
center is slowly moving too, huh?

67
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:40,597
It's probably closing in on
the royal palace on top of the.

68
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:41,510
the

69
00:04:41,593 --> 00:04:42,423
plateau.

70
00:04:42,506 --> 00:04:45,437
In other words, where Doflamingo
is fighting right now.

71
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:49,814
Unless we push toward the center,
we'll be shredded like everything else.

72
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:06,016
Now that we're in the midst of it,
I see that things are quite chaotic.

73
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:07,690
This way.

74
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:09,550
Cesaro!

75
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:13,717
Might I inquire where
you're going, Sir Zoro?

76
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:14,800
What do you mean?

77
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:15,920
Isn't it obvious?

78
00:05:16,180 --> 00:05:17,010
Huh?

79
00:05:17,093 --> 00:05:19,560
We're going to stop that thing.

80
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:21,470
There.

81
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:22,730
Where?

82
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:26,750
No!

83
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:35,700
What a surprise.

84
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:38,917
I never knew there were little
people here in Dressrosa.

85
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,118
I hope your arm turns out all right.

86
00:05:41,620 --> 00:05:45,914
They said it should be back in working
order once the blood flow returns.

87
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:46,880
Yeah, I know.

88
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,260
I'm a doctor.

89
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:53,500
When I saw that underground
port, one thing became clear.

90
00:05:58,200 --> 00:06:00,380
This is much bigger than one man.

91
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:04,435
Even if we defeat Doflamingo,
the battle won't be over.

92
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:08,860
But it will cause
ripples across the world.

93
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:13,540
And all eyes will be on you and Straw Hat.

94
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:18,760
Yeah, that was the plan.

95
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:39,800
4th gear, do tell.

96
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:41,380
That's right.

97
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:43,900
I gotta kick your ass in a hurry.

98
00:06:47,260 --> 00:06:49,580
It's nothing like second.

99
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:38,140
Oh, yeah!

100
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:49,100
Bounce man!

101
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:01,980
I'm sorry, is this supposed to be a joke?

102
00:08:02,340 --> 00:08:05,120
You certainly got big,
I'll give you that much.

103
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:07,217
Do you think a balloon scares me?

104
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:10,829
And here I thought you had some
secret strategy to win this.

105
00:08:11,020 --> 00:08:12,257
What are you going to do?

106
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:13,458
Bounce me to death?

107
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:16,557
You can't even stand on
your own two feet anymore.

108
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:20,522
How are you supposed to kick my
ass with a stupid power like that?

109
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:26,260
For two whole years, I
fought against wild animals.

110
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:30,360
As huge and savage as any
monster you could think of.

111
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:42,100
If I wanted to wrestle them to the ground,

112
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:46,560
I needed greater size
and greater bounciness.

113
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:53,420
And what good does elasticity do?

114
00:08:58,540 --> 00:09:00,080
Shut up!

115
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:08,900
Once I start, you won't
even be able to fight back!

116
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:16,020
Now my Gum-Gum!

117
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:19,090
Come!

118
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:24,590
Die!

119
00:09:53,020 --> 00:09:55,280
It's Doflamingo!

120
00:10:12,420 --> 00:10:16,497
everyone stand back
don't move what the hell

121
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:20,800
are you doing here i'd
like to know that myself

122
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:30,910
Hello?

123
00:10:30,993 --> 00:10:33,096
We'll end up hitting the breadcrumbs!

124
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:39,750
This is downtown.

125
00:10:39,833 --> 00:10:41,780
It really knocked me a long way.

126
00:10:54,220 --> 00:10:56,820
It's using elastic force to fly?

127
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:04,420
This one's my Gum-Gum!

128
00:11:07,860 --> 00:11:09,180
Rhino Schneider!

129
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:20,020
Somebody else showed up!

130
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:21,260
He's massive!

131
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:23,539
And it looks like he's strong, too!

132
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:34,940
He's a... giant... ball man?

133
00:11:44,260 --> 00:11:45,680
Little bastard.

134
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:50,037
He's hardening his skin with
armament Haki and using the

135
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:53,532
tensile force to multiply his
strength several times over.

136
00:11:57,940 --> 00:11:59,937
I'm not gonna lose to a ball.

137
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:01,820
I'm stronger than rubber.

138
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:19,720
I'm so sick of this crap!

139
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:35,180
I told you, didn't I?

140
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:38,780
Now that I'm using 4th
gear, you can't keep up!

141
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:42,320
Here I come, Mingo!

142
00:12:43,260 --> 00:12:45,966
Who the hell do you think
you're dealing with?

143
00:13:09,260 --> 00:13:12,280
Now, Gum-Gum!

144
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:19,380
To the red!

145
00:13:24,460 --> 00:13:25,290
Athlete!

146
00:13:32,180 --> 00:13:35,400
Even with the armor,
he's still like rubber.

147
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:38,200
You think that's going to work on me?

148
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:40,100
Not now!

149
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:43,350
Yeah.

150
00:13:43,433 --> 00:13:44,800
I can't believe this.

151
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,960
Don't you dare try and run away.

152
00:13:47,180 --> 00:13:49,356
You're going to get that ass kicking.

153
00:13:52,260 --> 00:13:53,460
What's happening?

154
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:55,120
It keeps going.

155
00:13:58,120 --> 00:14:00,140
Chase him down. Python!

156
00:14:01,860 --> 00:14:02,800
Damn it.

157
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:11,300
How far can his arm stretch?

158
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:13,420
Ahh!

159
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:24,780
Enough! Teach this!

160
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:28,660
And now comes on!

161
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,400
Culverin!

162
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:22,180
He got a beating! Doflamingo?

163
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:24,580
From a ball? How?

164
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:48,840
Hang on, who's that? He's strong. Wow.

165
00:15:49,220 --> 00:15:50,220
Knock him dead!

166
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:51,360
You can do it!

167
00:15:57,660 --> 00:15:59,500
Straw Hat? Yeah.

168
00:16:00,300 --> 00:16:01,620
He's so different now.

169
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:03,480
Is that him?

170
00:16:03,640 --> 00:16:05,346
I mean, it's hard to believe.

171
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:10,797
Why, if he can overpower
Doflamingo, he must be quite strong.

172
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:11,710
But...

173
00:16:11,793 --> 00:16:13,840
he's overusing his Haki.

174
00:16:16,060 --> 00:16:17,300
Oh, dear. Really?

175
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:25,020
Ah, there he is.

176
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:27,652
Guess they're playing somewhere else now.

177
00:16:28,020 --> 00:16:32,020
And after I went to all that trouble
to come over here and see them!

178
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:36,496
The captain of the first ship of the
Blackbeard Pirates, Jesus Burgess.

179
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:39,200
Looks like I found him. Chase them?

180
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:40,440
Or wait?

181
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:42,880
Either way, they're mine for sure.

182
00:16:43,260 --> 00:16:45,600
I'll get what I want, no matter what!

183
00:16:47,540 --> 00:16:48,370
Wee!

184
00:16:49,860 --> 00:16:50,690
I was right.

185
00:16:50,773 --> 00:16:51,817
He's after Luffy's group.

186
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:53,194
But what's his motive?

187
00:16:59,000 --> 00:16:59,830
Viola.

188
00:16:59,913 --> 00:17:02,841
His fight with Luffy is
all that remains, correct?

189
00:17:04,060 --> 00:17:04,937
That's right, Father.

190
00:17:05,020 --> 00:17:08,317
All of the top executives and their
underlings have been eliminated.

191
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:09,637
Only Doflamingo remains.

192
00:17:09,720 --> 00:17:11,640
Let's move, Tontanus!

193
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:13,080
Hurry it up!

194
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:16,460
We're on our way!

195
00:17:16,780 --> 00:17:20,960
Step up, or else you guys are
gonna be super dead in a minute!

196
00:17:28,820 --> 00:17:32,357
We managed to rescue all our friends
who were stranded in the factory.

197
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:33,440
We're good to go!

198
00:17:34,480 --> 00:17:35,310
Sweet!

199
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:43,300
Hey, the building's leaning over!

200
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:48,951
Froland, why is the Smile Factory the
only thing that's not getting cut off?

201
00:17:49,180 --> 00:17:50,320
Wait, it's not?

202
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:53,580
Right, the Sea Prism Stone.

203
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:54,820
Sea Prism?

204
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:57,977
Yeah, that's what the
walls are made out of.

205
00:17:58,060 --> 00:17:59,531
It's pretty strong stuff.

206
00:17:59,980 --> 00:18:04,940
Which means, the strings cut everything
else, but the factory won't crack.

207
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:07,200
Here, watch. Huh?

208
00:18:14,940 --> 00:18:16,640
We're just pushing it.

209
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:20,340
Hey, it's them! Cranky!

210
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:22,700
Ah! Sir Robot!

211
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:29,460
Saru Land, top that land!

212
00:18:29,780 --> 00:18:31,620
Uh, guys, what gives?

213
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:34,817
Center of the country is kind
of in the other direction.

214
00:18:34,900 --> 00:18:37,040
Want to run? Turn around.

215
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:38,810
What?

216
00:18:38,893 --> 00:18:39,723
We're not running.

217
00:18:39,860 --> 00:18:41,520
We want to stop the strings.

218
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:43,270
Stop them?

219
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:46,320
I didn't even think about that. Wow!

220
00:18:46,820 --> 00:18:48,020
That's amazing!

221
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:52,958
It's not over until Luffy settles
the score, but we can buy some time.

222
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:56,860
Oh, yeah!

223
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:21,781
Even with his armament active, he can still
expand and contract with such precision.

224
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:29,780
Armament and rubber
working in harmony, huh?

225
00:19:39,940 --> 00:19:42,600
If I take too long, I'll change back!

226
00:19:44,660 --> 00:19:48,719
It seems like you've figured out
how to use that ability pretty well.

227
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:51,607
But it must take a toll
on you after a while.

228
00:19:52,020 --> 00:19:53,800
I'm sure it has its risks.

229
00:19:56,560 --> 00:19:58,580
You're tired, aren't you?

230
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:00,509
How long can you hold out?

231
00:20:00,780 --> 00:20:04,440
You know...

232
00:20:04,900 --> 00:20:07,700
I can use my strings as much as I'd like.

233
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:09,230
Culverin!

234
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:10,960
Off what?

235
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:16,040
The ground?

236
00:20:16,260 --> 00:20:17,440
How did you do that?

237
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:21,060
Master, what have you done to this town?

238
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:24,020
Listen closely, rookie.

239
00:20:26,540 --> 00:20:29,080
My Devil Fruit's power ascended.

240
00:20:29,420 --> 00:20:31,777
They've reached a new horizon.

241
00:20:31,860 --> 00:20:34,180
A higher state known as Awakening.

242
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:43,070
Whoa!

243
00:20:43,153 --> 00:20:45,078
He turns the buildings into strings!

244
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:49,120
Awakening is extremely rare.

245
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:53,060
But with it, my strings can
affect more than just my own body.

246
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:54,910
Dear!

247
00:20:54,993 --> 00:20:56,937
His strings are all over the place!

248
00:20:57,020 --> 00:20:58,820
This can't be a parameathia!

249
00:20:59,100 --> 00:21:02,700
No matter which way you go,
there's more strings. Fun, right?

250
00:21:04,980 --> 00:21:08,039
At this rate, you won't
even be able to get near me.

251
00:21:17,300 --> 00:21:18,160
Tick-tock.

252
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:20,737
Any minute now, your
body's going to give out.

253
00:21:20,820 --> 00:21:22,680
And mine will keep on going.

254
00:21:46,440 --> 00:21:47,520
You won't quit.

255
00:21:49,700 --> 00:21:51,657
Hockey's about to run out, Straw Hat.

256
00:21:51,740 --> 00:21:54,328
That's when I'll deliver
the finishing blow!

257
00:21:58,180 --> 00:22:01,280
We have to run or let's just pop!

258
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:13,700
Oh no, Grandma!

259
00:22:14,880 --> 00:22:17,409
I thought I'd stand up
for you and make it!

260
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:19,380
I'm sorry.

261
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:24,540
I can't run anymore.

262
00:22:26,900 --> 00:22:29,940
Leave me and save yourself, dear.

263
00:22:30,320 --> 00:22:31,420
I won't do that!

264
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:33,326
I'm not going to abandon you!

265
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:36,360
Hurry, run.

266
00:22:36,600 --> 00:22:38,600
This is the end for me either way.

267
00:22:38,700 --> 00:22:39,840
Come on, get up!

268
00:22:40,200 --> 00:22:43,847
I'm telling you, I don't have
enough strength to run downtown.

269
00:22:43,960 --> 00:22:45,254
You should go quickly.

270
00:22:50,140 --> 00:22:50,970
People!

271
00:22:51,100 --> 00:22:52,520
We need help here!

272
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:55,260
All these patients, they can't get out!

273
00:22:55,500 --> 00:22:57,740
And we can't carry them by ourselves!

274
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:01,340
I've lost my son!

275
00:23:01,640 --> 00:23:03,240
He's wearing a Kuma shirt!

276
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:05,100
Have you seen him?

277
00:23:05,360 --> 00:23:06,520
Please, no!

278
00:23:06,920 --> 00:23:09,920
There must be someone who
can help me find my baby!

279
00:23:16,500 --> 00:23:18,676
Everybody's gonna die no matter what.

280
00:23:19,380 --> 00:23:20,520
It's pointless

281
00:23:24,700 --> 00:23:27,697
Even if we run you're stuck in the cage.

282
00:23:27,780 --> 00:23:32,780
Doflamingo will kill us anyway,
so it's easier to just give up

283
00:23:52,340 --> 00:23:54,460
Please, listen well.

284
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:57,817
It is on.

285
00:23:57,900 --> 00:24:01,160
King, rather, former king, Rick Dolgo III.

286
00:24:04,840 --> 00:24:06,280
What's going on?

287
00:24:06,580 --> 00:24:08,200
It's really him?

288
00:24:10,120 --> 00:24:12,380
As you can see, yes.

289
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:16,417
Because of the game that the current
King Doflamingo has forced upon us,

290
00:24:16,500 --> 00:24:20,380
We've been trapped inside this
birdcage with seemingly no escape.

291
00:24:21,480 --> 00:24:26,140
And, to make matters even more
bleak, the cage is rapidly shrinking,

292
00:24:26,620 --> 00:24:28,267
slicing everything in sight.

293
00:24:34,140 --> 00:24:34,970
Rick...

294
00:24:35,053 --> 00:24:37,280
This was thrust upon you so suddenly.

295
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:41,760
I'm sure your emotions
could barely keep up,

296
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:46,100
and now you struggle to survive
and protect your loved ones.

297
00:24:50,840 --> 00:24:54,280
This may feel like a
nightmare, but it's quite real,

298
00:24:54,620 --> 00:24:57,177
and this tragedy did not just begin today,

299
00:24:57,260 --> 00:25:01,500
because for a whole decade,
Dressrosa was already a birdcage,

300
00:25:01,740 --> 00:25:03,980
and all of us were being held inside,

301
00:25:04,280 --> 00:25:06,515
under the oppressive reign of pirates.

302
00:25:12,180 --> 00:25:15,020
For ten years now we have been puppets,

303
00:25:15,240 --> 00:25:18,400
constantly being manipulated
by the strings that they

304
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:21,790
pulled.

305
00:25:21,873 --> 00:25:23,520
Such has been our reality.

306
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:26,637
But soon that is going to change.

307
00:25:26,720 --> 00:25:30,860
The fear Don Quixote family,
whom we believe were unstoppable,

308
00:25:31,300 --> 00:25:34,557
have nearly been eliminated
by a group of mighty warriors

309
00:25:34,640 --> 00:25:37,581
who only happen to be
passing through our country.

310
00:25:38,380 --> 00:25:42,520
None of the executives are
left standing. Oh, really?

311
00:25:42,760 --> 00:25:44,260
Who could do that?

312
00:25:44,900 --> 00:25:46,760
I don't know, but it wasn't us.

313
00:25:46,980 --> 00:25:49,380
The final obstacle is him.

314
00:25:49,860 --> 00:25:53,080
The ruthless tyrant who has
Cheshrosa under his thumb.

315
00:25:53,620 --> 00:25:54,920
Do Flamingo.

316
00:26:05,120 --> 00:26:11,140
And the brave soul who is doing battle
with him is Luffy of the Straw Hat Pirates.

317
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:12,960
I believe he'll save us.

318
00:26:13,120 --> 00:26:15,657
He'll destroy this
birdcage once and for all.

319
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:19,100
That win or lose, it
will end in mere minutes.

320
00:26:19,660 --> 00:26:23,480
So try to survive until then,
no matter what it takes.

321
00:26:24,720 --> 00:26:29,360
Our dear country may be crumbling, but
I cannot allow you to go down with it.

322
00:26:29,720 --> 00:26:31,800
I implore you to keep running.

323
00:26:32,820 --> 00:26:36,420
Even if you run out of breath
or your legs are broken.

324
00:26:37,740 --> 00:26:40,460
For a few minutes, please try to survive.

325
00:26:48,320 --> 00:26:50,460
There is still hope for us.

326
00:26:50,740 --> 00:26:53,160
That is why you mustn't surrender yet.

327
00:27:01,800 --> 00:27:03,212
We'll do our best alone.

328
00:27:04,280 --> 00:27:05,560
Right. Good.

329
00:27:06,040 --> 00:27:07,620
Let's go! Run!

330
00:27:15,040 --> 00:27:15,870
Okay!

331
00:27:16,680 --> 00:27:17,510
Yeah.

332
00:27:19,160 --> 00:27:20,897
You should do what King Rick says.

333
00:27:20,980 --> 00:27:21,920
Don't give up.

334
00:27:22,100 --> 00:27:23,982
Let's all run downtown together.

335
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:25,320
Help the patients!

336
00:27:25,720 --> 00:27:26,720
Grab the beds!

337
00:27:33,960 --> 00:27:34,790
Here.

338
00:27:38,640 --> 00:27:39,470
Mummy!

339
00:27:44,460 --> 00:27:47,480
We have to survive
until the battle's over!

340
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:53,040
That Straw Hat roofer is going to put
Doflamingo in his place! I know it! Yeah!

341
00:27:58,780 --> 00:28:00,300
I said Bingo!

342
00:28:05,780 --> 00:28:08,340
Your demise is long overdue.

343
00:28:10,360 --> 00:28:12,400
There's not much time left.

344
00:28:12,520 --> 00:28:14,638
The whole town's starting to strike.

345
00:28:15,200 --> 00:28:17,000
Now billow white.

346
00:28:27,440 --> 00:28:28,500
It's over.

347
00:28:35,480 --> 00:28:37,560
I'll blow you away!

348
00:28:55,600 --> 00:28:57,600
You're mine now!

349
00:29:04,100 --> 00:29:06,720
I'm going to end this for good!

350
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:11,380
With my Gum-Gum!

351
00:29:18,720 --> 00:29:20,720
Leo Bazooka!

352
00:29:54,860 --> 00:29:57,200
He won.

353
00:29:59,420 --> 00:30:01,300
He beat the flamingo!
